{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Adversarial evaluation set (ADR-014 decision 1).  Seven threat classes plus multilingual/policy-suppression variants: direct prompt injection, indirect prompt injection (knowledge-article seed), system prompt probing, cross-tenant retrieval (foreign order/customer refs under a second tenant principal), tool-parameter injection (non-canonical resource ids re-authorized by the gateway), PII/secret exfiltration (payment card / phone / email / one-time code), malicious attachment text (text/plain payload must not be echoed), and multilingual injection variants.  Every case pins tenant/prompt/model/version/allowed tools and asserts the expected action/citation/redaction/canary outcome so a pass or fail is traceable to a fixed configuration.  Independent schema: golden/adversarial.json is validated by scripts/adversarial_schema.py, not by the golden validator (its strict expect-key check would reject the ADR-014 extension).",
